    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/temporary-jobs-on-campus-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Temporary Jobs On Campus",
      "description": "Temporary Jobs On Campus - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Temporary Jobs On Campus Temporary Jobs On Campus 496885 Boise, Idaho Classified Non-Classified/Professional Opening on: Oct 1 2026 Boise State University has frequent opportunities for short-term employment, either full or part time, that often can start within a few days. Types of work can include a wide variety of specialties in a number of different departments across campus, including: Administration and Office Support Skilled Trades and Technical Services Custodial and Facilities Maintenance IT Services and Project Opportunities Academic Support or Advising Health Sciences Specialists Communications, Marketing and Graphic Design Athletics Administration Support Specialties Albertsons Library Day and Evening Work If you would like to share your work experience with us and tell us how we can contact you, please click Apply Now. We will get in touch with you to let you know when we've found an opportunity that appears to match your background and experience. Please include your resume and any other supporting materials that can help us match you to a great opportunity on campus! Recommended Jobs Public Safety Officer Boise, Idaho Mid-Level, Safety and Security Director, Environmental Services Boise, Idaho Athletics, Environmental Safety, Mid-Level Assistant Producer, Idaho Matters Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Entry-Level, Marketing and Communications, Radio Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-professor-field-coordinator-bsw-program-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Field Coordinator BSW Program",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Field Coordinator BSW Program - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Clinical Assistant Professor - Field Coordinator BSW Program Clinical Assistant Professor - Field Coordinator BSW Program 499891 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Nov 3 2026 Closing on: Nov 30 2026 The Clinical Assistant Professor – Field Coordinator supports the School of Social Work’s field education program, with primary responsibility for students enrolled in the fully online BSW program. This 12-month position coordinates, develops, assesses, and manages practicum placements and agency partnerships across the United States. Responsibilities include teaching online field seminars; serving as a faculty field liaison; supporting students, field instructors, and agency partners throughout the practicum experience; and assisting with accreditation, compliance, training, and program assessment activities related to field education. The Field Coordinator collaborates closely with the Field Education Director and Assistant Director, Program Coordinators, faculty, and community partners to support student success and maintain high-quality field education experiences aligned with CSWE accreditation standards. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Boise State University is unable to sponsor an employment visa for this position. This position may be based in Boise, Idaho, or approved for remote work within the United States. The preferred start date is December 2026, though a January 2027 start may also be considered. Duties and Responsibilities: Coordinate and support practicum placements, agency partnerships, and field education activities for online BSW students. Serve as faculty liaison for assigned students and teach online and/or face-to-face field seminar courses. Recruit, develop, and maintain relationships with practicum agencies and field instructors nationwide. Support field instructors and students through training, consultation, problem-solving, and ongoing communication regarding practicum expectations and student progress. Assist with field education program assessment, accreditation compliance, curriculum implementation, and continuous improvement efforts. Maintain field education records, databases, forms, manuals, and related documentation. Evaluate practicum placements and assist in resolving student, agency, or field-related concerns. Participate in School of Social Work committees and other service activities as assigned. Collaborate with faculty and program leadership to support quality field education experiences and student success. The School: Housed within the College of Health Sciences at Boise State University, the School of Social Work prepares graduates in Idaho, the Pacific Northwest, and throughout the country for beginning and advanced social work practice. Our programs are rigorous and our faculty provide a comprehensive and interactive in-person and online education. Our curriculum is informed by a recognition of the critical importance of diversity and an understanding of cultural, political, and socio-historical contexts for social work education, practice, and research. Being a part of the College of Health Sciences provides numerous opportunities for collaborative interdisciplinary research and educational programming. Today the School has the largest graduate program at the University. The 280 undergraduate students and 539 graduate students (89 face-to-face and 450 online) are served by 23 full-time faculty. In addition to the undergraduate BSW program, the School also offers both the Full-Program MSW and the Advanced Standing MSW options. All social work programs have been reaffirmed for accreditation through February 2027 by the CSWE. About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop – a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Minimum qualifications: Master’s degree in Social Work and three years of relevant professional experience. Licensed Master Social Worker (LMSW). Experience working with students in field education or practicum settings. Experience working effectively in virtual and hybrid environments, including use of digital collaboration and learning management platforms. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain professional relationships in online learning environments. Preferred qualifications: Doctoral Degree in Social Work (PhD or DSW) Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW). Knowledge of social work ethics and Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) EPAS standards. Experience with online or hybrid delivery of social work education. Experience training, mentoring, or supporting students and field instructors. Familiarity with student information systems, databases, and standard office software applications. Knowledge of community-based resources and referral systems. Commitment to supporting inclusive learning and working environments. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to foster engagement and connection in virtual learning environments. Proficiency with learning management systems, virtual meeting platforms, and standard workplace software. Ability to manage documentation, data entry, and related administrative responsibilities. Ability to collaborate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and community partners. Required application materials: Cover letter Resume or CV Teaching philosophy statement Contact information for three professional references Closing Date: Review of applications will begin Sunday, November 15. The position will remain open to new applicants through Monday, November 30. For questions regarding this position, please contact Nicole Lang, Assistant Director of Field Education nicolelang@boisestate.edu . Salary and Benefits: Choose an option: Salary ranges from $68,000 to $73,000. Our standard faculty contract is a 12-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract, unless noted that the position is temporary. More information about faculty contract and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. See our full benefits page for more information Recommended Jobs Public Safety Officer Boise, Idaho Mid-Level, Safety and Security Director, Environmental Services Boise, Idaho Athletics, Environmental Safety, Mid-Level Assistant Producer, Idaho Matters Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Entry-Level, Marketing and Communications, Radio Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
