    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/provost-and-vice-president-for-academic-affairs-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs 499822 Boise, Idaho Faculty Non-Classified/Professional Opening on: Aug 24 2026 Boise State University seeks a strategic, forward-looking academic leader to serve as its next Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs. Reporting directly to the President, the Provost serves as the university’s Chief Academic Officer and, through a phased integration, will assume oversight of Student Affairs and Enrollment Management. This expanded portfolio presents a unique opportunity to advance Boise State’s academic, research, and student success priorities. As Idaho’s largest public university, Boise State serves more than 28,500 students and offers a broad portfolio of undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs. Over the past several years, the institution has experienced record enrollment growth, significant increases in student retention and graduation rates, and substantial expansion in research productivity and doctoral education. A metropolitan research university deeply connected to the economic and workforce needs of Idaho, Boise State has emerged as a national model for integrating student success, innovation, community engagement, and applied research, while positioning itself for Carnegie R1 research university classification. At a time of significant change across higher education and within the university, Boise State seeks a provost who can build trust, foster collaboration, and strengthen relationships across the university community. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to transparent communication, shared governance, and thoughtful leadership that balances innovation with institutional stability. Boise State has experienced significant growth in research activity, doctoral education, enrollment, and national visibility, establishing itself as one of the nation’s rising public universities. The next Provost will help shape the institution’s next chapter, building on this momentum to advance student success, expand scholarly impact, strengthen academic quality, and foster innovation across the university. Working closely with the President, deans, faculty, and university leadership, the Provost will guide the continued evolution of Boise State as a premier student-success driven, public research university. This includes advancing innovation in teaching and learning; strengthening alignment among academic programs, workforce needs, research and creative activity, and community impact; stewarding resources in support of academic priorities and long-term sustainability; and articulating the value of a Boise State education for students, families, and the state of Idaho. Boise State seeks an accomplished academic leader with an earned doctorate or terminal degree, a record of scholarly achievement meriting appointment as a full professor, and significant senior leadership experience. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to shared governance, academic excellence, research growth, faculty engagement, and student success, along with the strategic vision, operational expertise, and collaborative leadership necessary to guide a complex public university through a period of continued growth and opportunity. All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications should include, as two separate documents, a CV and a letter of interest addressing the themes in the leadership profile. WittKieffer is assisting Boise State University in this search. For fullest consideration, candidate materials should be received by November 13, 2026. Application materials should be submitted through WittKieffer’s candidate portal using the buttons above or below. Nominations and inquiries can be directed to: Zachary A. Smith, Ph.D., Lauren Bruce-Stets, and Tyler Workman at BoiseStateProvost@wittkieffer.com . Back to job search Recommended Jobs Public Safety Officer Boise, Idaho Mid-Level, Safety and Security Director, Environmental Services Boise, Idaho Athletics, Environmental Safety, Mid-Level Assistant Producer, Idaho Matters Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Entry-Level, Marketing and Communications, Radio Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-mathematics-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Mathematics - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Teaching Professor - Mathematics Assistant Teaching Professor - Mathematics 499936 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Oct 21 2026 Closing on: Dec 18 2026 The Department of Mathematics at Boise State University invites applications for a dynamic Assistant Teaching Professor specializing in calculus, beginning August 2027. We are looking for an experienced and collaborative mathematics instructor who is passionate about teaching and eager to make a lasting impact on our calculus program. In a non-tenure track faculty position with opportunities for promotion, you will teach calculus courses (typically 3 (4-credit) classes per semester, 80% of workload) and serve as the lead coordinator for single-variable calculus, guiding a community of instructors, fostering active and inclusive learning environments for students, and partnering with stakeholders. This is a high-impact position with a central role in helping thousands of undergraduate students thrive at Boise State. Department overview: Home to an active community of educators and researchers, the Department of Mathematics is central to Boise State University's academic and scientific mission. We deliver high quality degree programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels, encompassing pure and applied mathematics, statistics, and mathematics education. We also provide the foundational mathematical coursework for over 50 degree pathways. Our department has a proud tradition of pioneering evidence-based curricular reforms, coordinated course design, award-winning teaching, and collaborative efforts to support student persistence and achievement. From our base along the Boise River in the Mathematics Building, our faculty and staff foster a welcoming, collegial environment where teaching excellence, innovative pedagogy, and meaningful student mentorship are deeply valued and supported. About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop – a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Minimum qualifications: Earned doctorate in mathematics, mathematics education, or a closely related field by August 1, 2027; OR earned master’s degree in mathematics, mathematics education, or a closely related field by August 1, 2027 with at least 8 years of teaching experience. At least 2 years of experience teaching calculus as lead instructor in a post-secondary setting. Preferred qualifications: Extensive knowledge of undergraduate mathematics, especially content relevant to the teaching and learning of calculus. Experience in mathematics course design and course material development. Experience promoting student success in higher education, including implementing evidence-based instructional strategies and collaboration with partners. Experience collaborating in undergraduate mathematics instruction, such as coordinated multi-section courses. Experience mentoring and supporting mathematics instructors, including adjunct faculty and new instructors. Experience using course technology, including learning management systems and online practice systems. Required application materials: Cover Letter: Specifically addressing the minimum and preferred qualifications, as well as your background and interest in the position. Curriculum Vitae (CV): Including your full educational and employment history with dates. Teaching Statement: Detailing your pedagogical approach, background and experience teaching mathematics, and methods for fostering student success in introductory college-level mathematics. Contact Information for Three Professional References: Including name, job title, email address, and phone number. Closing Date: The position will close for new applicants on December 18, 2026. For questions regarding this position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Joe Champion, joechampion@boisestate.edu . Salary and Benefits: The salary for this position is set at $58,656. Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract, unless noted that the position is temporary. More information about faculty contract and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. See our full benefits page for more information Back to job search Recommended Jobs Public Safety Officer Boise, Idaho Mid-Level, Safety and Security Director, Environmental Services Boise, Idaho Athletics, Environmental Safety, Mid-Level Assistant Producer, Idaho Matters Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Entry-Level, Marketing and Communications, Radio Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and 