    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-statistics-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Statistics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Statistics - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Statistics Assistant Professor of Statistics 499921 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Oct 16 2026 The Department of Mathematics at Boise State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Statistics starting in fall 2027. We seek candidates whose research focuses on biostatistics, computational statistics, statistical learning, data science, or a closely related area and who have strong potential for collaboration with researchers affiliated with the Biomedical Research Institute (BRI) at Boise State University. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to both research and teaching. The successful candidate will contribute to the department’s existing statistics curriculum, develop new courses within their area of expertise, and build an externally funded research program that provides opportunities for graduate student training and mentorship. This position is part of Boise State University's interdisciplinary Biomolecular Sciences Cluster Hire Initiative, with open positions in the departments of Biological Sciences, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Mathematics, and Physics. The goal is to support a cohort of scientists with the potential to create new interdisciplinary research collaborations, support graduate education and the growth of doctoral programs, position Boise State for long-term research distinction, and build on existing institutional strengths. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose research has biomedical applications and strong potential to attract NIH and other externally sponsored research funding. Candidates should describe the potential for their research to contribute to at least one of the existing or emerging areas of interdisciplinary strength at Boise State University, including Matrix Biology COBRE , the Convergent Engineering and Biomolecular Science (CEBS) COBRE , Healthy Idaho Clinical and Translational Research (CTR-D) Program , Neuroscience , Cancer Research, and Quantum Information Science. Applicants should also discuss how their research could leverage Boise State's shared instrumentation, core facilities (BRCF and FaCT Cores), and collaborative research infrastructure, including resources available through the Biomedical Research Institute, while contributing to a collaborative environment that advances scientific discovery, graduate education, and externally funded research. Due to the intrinsic impact of these topics, the new hire is expected to have a strong knowledge of modern statistical and computational methods and a demonstrated interest in applications related to biomedical sciences, health sciences, and other interdisciplinary research areas. Department Overview: The Department of Mathematics at Boise State University is strongly committed to excellence in research, teaching, and service. We offer B.S. and M.S. degrees in Mathematics with several emphasis areas, including statistics. The department also co-leads the Computing Ph.D. program within the School of Computing, which offers emphasis areas in data science, artificial intelligence, computational math, science and engineering, computer science, and cybersecurity. Faculty share teaching strategies and work together to improve the student experience, and the department places a strong emphasis on mentoring graduate students. The department also supports faculty success through mentoring and professional development. Research spans many areas of the mathematical sciences, providing opportunities for collaboration within the department, across Boise State, and with researchers at other institutions. Faculty have access to substantial computational resources through Boise State’s Research Computing department, which operates two high-performance computing clusters: Borah, a 40-node CPU and 20-node GPU cluster with 3.2 petabytes of storage, and Lemhi, a 504-node CPU cluster with 1.3 petabytes of storage. Research Computing also provides research, training, and classroom support to faculty, staff, and students. About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop – a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Statistics, Biostatistics, or a closely related field by the time of appointment Preferred Qualifications: A strong record of research accomplishments appropriate to the candidate’s career stage, including peer-reviewed publications, and a promising research agenda with potential for extramural funding. Evidence of the ability to teach statistics courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, effective teaching, and a commitment to supporting student learning and continued growth as an instructor. Experience or strong interest in interdisciplinary research that complements the Biomolecular Sciences Cluster Hire Initiative, with potential to collaborate or consult through the Biomedical Research Institute in areas such as biostatistics, quantitative biology, biomedical data science, computational modeling, biomedical imaging, statistical genomics, or related fields. Experience or demonstrated potential in student mentoring, including mentoring Ph.D. students in Boise State’s interdisciplinary doctoral programs, particularly those pursuing the Data Science or Artificial Intelligence emphases within the Ph.D. in Computing. Required Application Materials: All of the following materials must be submitted electronically via www.mathjobs.org : AMS Standard Cover Sheet A letter of application describing your interest in the position, your relevant experience and qualifications, and how your background aligns with the preferred qualifications. CV including publications and employment history (and dates of employment) Statement on research interests, accomplishments and future plans Statement on teaching experience, interests, and philosophy Graduate transcripts At least three letters of recommendation, one of which must address teaching in some depth In addition, to be considered for this position, please submit the application items 2 and 3 under the job posting listed on the Boise State University Careers page. Closing Date: Review of applications will begin on November 27, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions regarding this position please contact Dr. Kyungduk Ko (kyungdukko@boisestate.edu) Salary and Benefits: The salary for the 9-month academic year starts at $75,000, commensurate with experience. Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract, unless noted that the position is temporary. More information about faculty contract and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents See our full benefits page for more information Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 0c557877 Last Name (required) 30dbf10f Email (required) 844dd9a5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Public Safety Officer Boise, Idaho Mid-Level, Safety and Security Director, Environmental Services Boise, Idaho Athletics, Environmental Safety, Mid-Level Assistant Producer, Idaho Matters Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Entry-Level, Marketing and Communications, Radio Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0c5beb1f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 41af629b Last Name (required) 89132d66 Email (required) f1f6276e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
