    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/lecturer-1-mathematics-and-statistics-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer 1 - Mathematics and Statistics",
      "description": "Lecturer 1 - Mathematics and Statistics - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Lecturer 1 - Mathematics and Statistics Lecturer 1 - Mathematics and Statistics 499916 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Oct 13 2026 Position Overview and Responsibilities: The Department of Mathematics at Boise State University invites applications for a full-time non-tenure track lecturer in Mathematics and Statistics, with an anticipated start date in August 2027. The successful candidate will play a central role in delivering high-quality introductory statistics instruction in both online and in-person formats, and will contribute to the development and ongoing improvement of online statistics courses, including course materials and instructional practices. The standard teaching assignment is 24 credits across the fall and spring semesters, typically four classes per semester. Summer teaching opportunities are typically available, and interest in teaching during the summer is welcomed. Because the position includes regular in-person teaching and departmental service, the successful candidate must be able to work on campus in Boise. There is no research expectation associated with the position. Expectations of the position include: Teach online courses that support Boise State’s Online Degree Program. The program’s current and anticipated need is for sections of MATH 153, Statistical Reasoning, although future assignments may include other mathematics or statistics courses. Contribute to the development and ongoing improvement of online statistics courses, including course materials and instructional practices. Provide effective, student-centered instruction and establish accessible and welcoming learning environments. Use appropriate learning-management, homework, and instructional technologies to support student learning. Maintain consistency in course learning outcomes and academic expectations across online and in-person sections of introductory statistics. Collaborate with colleagues in the Department of Mathematics and with Online Degree Program partners on course delivery and program needs. Participate in institutional service activities such as course development and service on department committees. Minimum qualifications: Master’s degree or higher in mathematics, math education, statistics or a closely related field. Demonstrated experience in at least one of the following: Teaching introductory statistics at the college level. Teaching college-level courses in an online format. Experience using a learning-management system such as Canvas and online homework or assessment tools such as WebAssign. Ability to work on campus in Boise. Preferred qualifications: Experience teaching introductory statistics in an online format. Experience developing, revising, or maintaining online courses. Demonstrated effective teaching practices that support student learning. Experience collaborating with faculty and program partners to align curriculum. Excellent oral and written communication skills. To apply: Submit the following materials in Page Up Letter of application indicating how your qualifications and interests would fit with the position description CV including employment history (and dates of employment) Unofficial graduate transcript Statement describing teaching experience, interests, and philosophy Contact information for three professional references Review of applications will begin on December 11, 2026. For full consideration, please submit materials by that date. Contact: For questions about this position contact Megan Null at MeganMNull@boisestate.edu . Salary and Benefits: Salary starts at $56,118 and is commensurate with experience. Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract. More information about faculty contract and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. See our full benefits page for more information About Boise State University: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop – a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 84bd23b7 Last Name (required) 7b7e78d6 Email (required) 324fd4aa Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Public Safety Officer Boise, Idaho Mid-Level, Safety and Security Director, Environmental Services Boise, Idaho Athletics, Environmental Safety, Mid-Level Assistant Producer, Idaho Matters Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Entry-Level, Marketing and Communications, Radio Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 45bef3d3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 1473f427 Last Name (required) 47ab6737 Email (required) b1bbe315 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
